arxiv-2201-04601.description:
A 2022 arXiv research paper by Solomon Huang, Tommy Murphy, Thanh Nhan Phan. We adapt the work of Hall to find quasi-Einstein metrics on sphere bundles over products of Fano Kähler–Einstein manifolds, as well as bundles where only one end is blown down. Introduction

In Wang–Wang
[
6
]
, Hermitian–Einstein manifolds were constructed via a Kaluza–Klein bundle ansatz, on (i)
\mathbb{S}^{2}
-bundles over products of Fano Kähler–Einstein manifolds, and (ii)
\mathbb{R}P^{2}
-bundles over products of Fano Kähler–Einstein manifolds. In subsequent years (i) was generalized in various directions.
